{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me","id":1172699,"title":"Lunar martial artists just got a lot more interesting to me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-02T11:54:40-08:00","id":1172699,"title":"Lunar martial artists just got a lot more interesting to me","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you planned a new way for Lunars to interact with MA?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1172614#post1172614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can combo them with all their native Charms, which is pretty darn strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, &quot;pretty darn strong&quot; feels like an understatement. Solars with Mastery VS Lunar mixing MA with native Charms will likely lead to some damn amazing kung fu duels.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T12:12:35-08:00","id":1172706,"title":"","content":"Also consider this applies to all Attribute-based Exalts, meaning Alchemicals and Liminals can do this as well. Body horror kung fu, anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T13:14:53-08:00","id":1172718,"title":"","content":"(I'll add the obvious caveat that if this ends up being broken in playtesting, we'll change it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":22}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T13:50:30-08:00","id":1172729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me#post1172699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, &quot;pretty darn strong&quot; feels like an understatement. Solars with Mastery VS Lunar mixing MA with native Charms will likely lead to some damn amazing kung fu duels.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is and it isn't.<br /> As you point out, Lunars can mix MA with their Dex charms (of course; the reason you can't combine Brawl and Martial Arts charms is that it's impossible to roll Brawl and Martial Arts at the same time. Whereas, of course you roll Dex+Martial Arts, and so can apply both Martial Arts and Dex), but Solars just have better MA charms.<br /> <br /> Also, don't forget that Lunars can't use MA when in animal form (not sure about DBT). <br /> <br /> So, there might be some good synergies combining MA and Dex charms (and, of course, MA and Strength charms, MA and Stamina charms, etc, but Solars can also use Resistance and MA charms combined to boost their soak or whatever, so that's not a Lunar advantage), but MA is, otherwise, not a particularly strong option for Lunars. <br /> <br /> Honestly, while of course I haven't seem them playtested, I suspect Lunars need some particular reason to take MA*, or it'd be a very subpar, and thus rather rare, choice, compared to native Lunar charms which can be used while you're a Tyrant Lizard.<br /> <br /> *Besides Lunar XP, I guess. But no idea how that will work, so can't really comment.<br /> <br /> Which is a pity, because obviously Snake-totem Lunar with Snake style/Tiger-totem Lunar with Tiger style/Crane-totem Lunar with Crane style is too appropriate a character to nerf.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also... the fact that you can't combine Brawl with MA (or Melee with MA), except that, in certain situations, you can (I mean that you can attack with MA and parry with Melee) is quite confusing for some players.<br /> So saying &quot;you can't use MA charms on a Dex+Martial Arts roll if you also use a Dex charm&quot; might be even worse. It's just easier to say you can use (and could be mechanically interesting**).<br /> <br /> <br /> **As you say, I think it'd be fun to see the Solar with stronger MA fight the Lunar who has weaker MA, but combines them easier with their own charms for unique combos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T13:53:50-08:00","id":1172731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172718#post1172718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'll add the obvious caveat that if this ends up being broken in playtesting, we'll change it)</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, I already had that in mind, but it is better to have shitstorm-prevention-prana activated from the outset XD<br /> <br /> And I can certainly see the potential for things to end up broken. Since Lunars are being designed not to feel really left behind in mixed group with Solars, it is not hard to imagine stupidly strong combinations cropping up when mixed with MA, especially with the breadth of possibilities involved. I mean, it is very likely that, even if it turns out fine in playtest, someone is gonna eventually find a couple edge cases that end up too strong.<br /> <br /> I wonder if pacing of power growth might be an issue. For Ability-based Exalts, while they can invest in combat Charms that can synergize with MA bought with splat-name XP, Atribute-based Exalts get more bang for their buck that way by being able to mix it up much better. Then again, Solars get Supernal Abilities, so they can skip ahead on the power curve, so it is probably not an issue.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T14:02:51-08:00","id":1172738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172731#post1172731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haha, I already had that in mind</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\">techniiiiiiiques <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T14:37:59-08:00","id":1172754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172729#post1172729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, don't forget that Lunars can't use MA when in animal form (not sure about DBT).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this confirmed or is it one of those things that was the case in 2e and people are just assuming it still is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T15:04:45-08:00","id":1172762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172754#post1172754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this confirmed or is it one of those things that was the case in 2e and people are just assuming it still is?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the last word on the subject in 3E that I know of. To prevent weird stuff like Tyrant Lizards with oversized stat pools interacting with Charms not designed for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T15:38:20-08:00","id":1172774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ren9077</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172762#post1172762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was the last word on the subject in 3E that I know of. To prevent weird stuff like Tyrant Lizards with oversized stat pools interacting with Charms not designed for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also removes the need to nail down an animal's exact Attributes; this way, you generally will never roll Martial Arts while in an animal form, so it doesn't matter what their Dexterity is.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, since Lunar Exalted have amazing potential for unarmed combat just by using animal forms, and since Martial Arts generally don't mix with animal forms unless specifically design to work for inhuman forms...<br /> <br /> Seems to me that the Styles which offer the most use to Lunar Exalted are those that focus heavily on weapons, so that when a Lunar wants to use a weapon instead of claws, he's got as many tricks as possible for that weapon.<br /> <br /> Then there are Styles like White Veil, Black Claw, and Dreaming Pearl Courtesan, for a Lunar who wants to fuck things up while also sticking entirely to a human form, in order to hide her nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T16:21:08-08:00","id":1172795,"title":"","content":"Having thought about it, I think one of the implications of this that matters the most to me personally is the possibility that it will be an outstanding instance of Lunar power expressed primarily in superhuman terms.<br /> <br /> \u200bDon't get me wrong, I'm a big advocate for the animal and predator and shapeshifting imagery, but there are still some places where I think it's good for Lunar power to be focused on superhuman accomplishment, and I think being able to combine their power with Martial Arts could be a strong example of this.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, if they end up having a lot of predator or shapeshifting stuff that combines with them as well, it might also represent an instance in which Lunars are able to give a unique spin, whether in execution or visuals, on something that is otherwise common between the other Exalted, which also seems like it could be a good way to characterize them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T16:44:37-08:00","id":1172800,"title":"","content":"As I've said before... I want to be able to make Morgiana from Magi as a Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T16:46:07-08:00","id":1172801,"title":"","content":"Given the glee of being able to combo charms, imagine the mote cost for that. Sure you can go nova but the mote pool would most probably run empty after that spectacular display.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21242-charonferryman","name":"CharonFerryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T16:59:51-08:00","id":1172805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CharonFerryman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172801#post1172801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the glee of being able to combo charms, imagine the mote cost for that. Sure you can go nova but the mote pool would most probably run empty after that spectacular display.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Exalted aren't best-served by throwing every available Charm onto every attack, sure. On the other hand, having a few bread-and-butter style Charms to mix into your options for Martial Arts attacks, or the opportunity to sneak in some nasty esoteric Lunar stuff with your Martial Arts, can certainly make a fight with a Lunar martial artist challenging and distinct from a Solar or Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Plus, the <i>Abracapocalypse</i> solution is occasionally appropriate and hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4596-ren9077","name":"Ren9077","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"593"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T17:20:00-08:00","id":1172807,"title":"","content":"I think Lunar MA could get very cool inspirations from non-chinese martial traditions. I know there are the typical animal styles, but in the past, people have debated about how Lunars didn't need to emulate creatures they can take the shape of.<br /> <br /> African, polynesian, european, and even native american combat systems could work really well as inspirations for the type of styles that the Lunars have created through thery history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T19:57:41-08:00","id":1172840,"title":"","content":"Speaking of how Lunars interact with certain mechanics. Don't they lose access to Evocations in their Warform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T20:08:52-08:00","id":1172844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nilihum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172840#post1172840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of how Lunars interact with certain mechanics. Don't they lose access to Evocations in their Warform.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As per a vance tweet, they count as one level lower in Resonance. I personally would assume that Dissonant Evocations just stay Dissonant, because 100% losing an evocation seems kinda lame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T22:39:35-08:00","id":1172930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172844#post1172844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> As per a vance tweet, they count as one level lower in Resonance. I personally would assume that Dissonant Evocations just stay Dissonant, because 100% losing an evocation seems kinda lame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars aren't Dissonant with anything normally, so not really an issue. In Warform they'd be downgraded to Normal with Moonsilver and Dissonant with everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T23:55:18-08:00","id":1172938,"title":"","content":"I was never interested in Lunars before (i kinda thought of them as just &quot;werewolf splat taped on because White Wolf&quot;) but now that we are doing the Predator/ShapeShifter/Witch thing I'm starting to get interested in them. The Enkidu vibe really shines through a lot this time, and I'm really happy we are differentiating them from Solars mechanically.<br /> <br /> Hell, I actually would consider not being a GLORIOUS SOLAR for once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T00:48:17-08:00","id":1172944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172930#post1172930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lunars aren't Dissonant with anything normally, so not really an issue. In Warform they'd be downgraded to Normal with Moonsilver and Dissonant with everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, sounds like a good reason to go Warform-Bare knuckle Native charmset-enhanced Martial Arts then...<br /> <br /> Edit: I missed my chance to say Bear Knuckle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 01-03-2018, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T10:09:24-08:00","id":1173028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172944#post1172944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, sounds like a good reason to go Warform-Bare knuckle Native charmset-enhanced Martial Arts then...<br /> <br /> Edit: I missed my chance to say Bear Knuckle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, bear knuckles. For when you need to pry some guy's face off like that last flap of skin is a hinge, and then throw his comrades into the air until they land on trees and it looks like the Red Talons were decorating a macabre parody of Christmas.<br /> <br /> (See also Golden Kamuy vol. 2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T16:37:59-08:00","id":1173112,"title":"","content":"Where are you going to get this information?<br /> <br /> And why would a Lunar become dissonant with moonsilver under any circumstance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T17:05:50-08:00","id":1173117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173112#post1173112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you going to get this information?<br /> <br /> And why would a Lunar become dissonant with moonsilver under any circumstance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure which AMA the info came from, but being Resonant with Moonsilver to start with means that Lunars are never dissonant, just not Resonant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T17:06:23-08:00","id":1173118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173112#post1173112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you going to get this information?<br /> <br /> And why would a Lunar become dissonant with moonsilver under any circumstance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure which AMA the info came from, but being Resonant with Moonsilver to start with means that Lunars are never dissonant, just not Resonant in Deadly Beastman.<br /> <br /> Edits: apologies for the double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-03T21:32:54-08:00","id":1173158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173118#post1173118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure which AMA the info came from, but being Resonant with Moonsilver to start with means that Lunars are never dissonant, just not Resonant in Deadly Beastman.<br /> <br /> Edits: apologies for the double post.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not from an AMA, but from Arms of the Chosen, which introduced the Dissonant/Neutral/Resonant scheme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T01:10:56-08:00","id":1173174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173158#post1173158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not from an AMA, but from Arms of the Chosen, which introduced the Dissonant/Neutral/Resonant scheme.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the information on Lunars' usual affinity for Evocations of the various Magical Mateials is indeed in Arms, Prototype00 is talking about &quot;Lunars in DBT degrade their affinity to Evocations by one step&quot;, which I'm pretty sure is not in Arms (at least, I just searched the document for &quot;Deadly Beastman&quot; and found nothing...). It is likely either in the Aks the Devs thread, or Vance's Twitter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T02:21:30-08:00","id":1173181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173112#post1173112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you going to get this information?<br /> <br /> And why would a Lunar become dissonant with moonsilver under any circumstance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many moons ago there was some Dev-talk on how Lunars might have some <i>trade off </i>on access to Evocations when in their Deadly Beastfolk Transformation; to prevent One-True-Building. Apparently, that's still a plan, and the most recent Developer thoughts are to tie it in with the Resonance mechanics introduced in Arms of the Chosen.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nilihum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172840#post1172840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of how Lunars interact with certain mechanics. Don't they lose access to Evocations in their Warform.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172844#post1172844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per a <b>Vance tweet</b>, they count as one level lower in Resonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 01-04-2018, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T08:59:20-08:00","id":1173230,"title":"","content":"I hope that Lunars retain access to MA Charms in War Form at least, because if playing a giant mantis with Mantis Style is wrong then I don't want to be right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T09:02:25-08:00","id":1173231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173112#post1173112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And why would a Lunar become dissonant with moonsilver under any circumstance?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don\u2019t. If the downgrade in Resonance info is still accurate, they\u2019d go from Resonant to Normal with Moonsilver while in Warform, and Normal to Dissonant with everything else. They\u2019d remain oriented toward Moonsilver in that form, just less gifted with tool use compared to their human forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T09:07:23-08:00","id":1173234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173230#post1173230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that Lunars retain access to MA Charms in War Form at least, because if playing a giant mantis with Mantis Style is wrong then I don't want to be right.</div> </div> </div> </div>War Forms are still basically built and run like human forms, unlike animal forms which are so different they are better represented with Quick Character dice pools and special Merits.<br /> <br /> Since War Forms ought to still have the Lunar's basic, numerically-rated traits, they should be compatible with Martial Art Form Charms, which are designed to work with humanoid forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T11:42:57-08:00","id":1173271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173234#post1173234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">War Forms are still basically built and run like human forms, unlike animal forms which are so different they are better represented with Quick Character dice pools and special Merits.<br /> <br /> Since War Forms ought to still have the Lunar's basic, numerically-rated traits, they should be compatible with Martial Art Form Charms, which are designed to work with humanoid forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine there might even be some custom lunar MA styles meant for use with things only a lunar could use properly without some sorcerous workings/ cybernetic enhancements tagged on. Things like needing a prehensile tail perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:00:20-08:00","id":1173275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173271#post1173271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine there might even be some custom lunar MA styles meant for use with things only a lunar could use properly without some sorcerous workings/ cybernetic enhancements tagged on. Things like needing a prehensile tail perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d be totally down for the 3E versions of the 2E\u2019s Dragon King Martial Arts Styles being Lunar oriented instead (they\u2019d get more use that way). One geared to aerial combat and wing flurries, one to aquatic combat, and to extra limbs, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:06:25-08:00","id":1173276,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about some of the possible implications of this. Would it represent a limitation on what Lunar Charms can be, or does it just mean that Lunars get a dispensation that nobody else does. For instance, would there be Dexterity Charms to split attacks between multiple targets that could work with Martial Arts?<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, I imagine that if playtesting reveals it to be broken, the first solution is to use a Keyword to set aside the ones that are compatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:14:37-08:00","id":1173278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173276#post1173276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking about some of the possible implications of this. Would it represent a limitation on what Lunar Charms can be, or does it just mean that Lunars get a dispensation that nobody else does. For instance, would there be Dexterity Charms to split attacks between multiple targets that could work with Martial Arts?<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, I imagine that if playtesting reveals it to be broken, the first solution is to use a Keyword to set aside the ones that are compatible.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per the devs, it's intended for all Exalts with Attribute-based Charms, which at the moment is Lunars, Liminals and Alchemicals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:18:01-08:00","id":1173279,"title":"","content":"Weren't the Dragon King Martial Arts all still something that human characters could do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:18:15-08:00","id":1173280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173278#post1173278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As per the devs, it's intended for all Exalts with Attribute-based Charms, which at the moment is Lunars, Liminals and Alchemicals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren\u2019t Getimians also confirmed as Attribute based?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:19:08-08:00","id":1173282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173278#post1173278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As per the devs, it's intended for all Exalts with Attribute-based Charms, which at the moment is Lunars, Liminals and Alchemicals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't really address the substance of my question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:22:28-08:00","id":1173285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173279#post1173279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't the Dragon King Martial Arts all still something that human characters could do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they were in a supplement most people with no interest in Dragon Kings wouldn\u2019t see or use, and thanks to being Terrestrial level* Lunar characters (who were the most likely to take morphological advantage) were unlikely to take interest. Obviously that latter point isn\u2019t a problem in 3E.<br /> <br /> * Eye of Heaven was the Celestial level exception, and I hope to see it come back as a Solar oriented Style with its sacrifice to the Sun apex charm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:33:22-08:00","id":1173286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173285#post1173285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but they were in a supplement most people with no interest in Dragon Kings wouldn\u2019t see or use, and thanks to being Terrestrial level* Lunar characters (who were the most likely to take morphological advantage) were unlikely to take interest. Obviously that latter point isn\u2019t a problem in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAre you proposing that if the Styles had been put in a different book, they would have actually been written as something that the majority of players would be unable to use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:33:27-08:00","id":1173287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173280#post1173280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren\u2019t Getimians also confirmed as Attribute based?</div> </div> </div> </div>They were. Which sheds some light on their particular advantages with SMAs.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:57:00-08:00","id":1173293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1172718#post1172718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I'll add the obvious caveat that if this ends up being broken in playtesting, we'll change it)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seemed really god damn strong when I tried it with my own version of Alchemicals. Mainly because you need to ask yourself if your native charms do things better already. <br /> <br /> May be different for Lunars, mainly because charms there are one shot pops whereas Alchemicals can submod charms into beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:23:38-08:00","id":1173302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173276#post1173276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking about some of the possible implications of this. Would it represent a limitation on what Lunar Charms can be, or does it just mean that Lunars get a dispensation that nobody else does. For instance, would there be Dexterity Charms to split attacks between multiple targets that could work with Martial Arts?<br /> <br /> \u200bStill, I imagine that if playtesting reveals it to be broken, the first solution is to use a Keyword to set aside the ones that are compatible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, this also touches on another possible mild issue. Why use brawl? I imagine that this is yet another reason why the martial artist merit would prove a mild balancing feature, but honestly, brawl doesn't provide charms, but martial arts do.<br /> <br /> The worst case scenario I can see is that DBT weakens your mastery level and certain combat charms have upgrades when in DBT. Of course I'd be pushing for being able to use martial arts in the iconic lunar combat mode but at the same time...<br /> <br /> Hm. I have no idea how to avoid martial arts being too good but also worthwhile to have. The combo capability is just really potent, like crazy potent. Add in that if Lunars have Lunar XP, then they can double dip into combat charms and martial arts charms...<br /> <br /> And since martial arts charms are balanced around other exalted, we're more likely to see Lunar charms have to be designed around martial arts, which might end up having martial arts being a missing piece to the lunar charmset.<br /> <br /> That said, I already mentioned a possible solution: Deadly Beastman Transformation might have Lunar practitioners use charms at Terrestrial level instead but many charms have bonuses when in DBT. Now this doesn't remove the option of karate bug monsterman, but it does discourage it enough to give clear intended combat styles and modes.<br /> <br /> I don't know. I'm rambling. I will say I am mildly concerned that Lunar charmsets might feel incomplete because they have to be designed around working with martial arts. My issue isn't that martial arts is good, its that I don't want the only way to make a combat lunar end up being &quot;take martial arts&quot;.<br /> <br /> So outside of the merit cost, why should a lunar use brawl?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:30:58-08:00","id":1173303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173302#post1173302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, this also touches on another possible mild issue. Why use brawl? I imagine that this is yet another reason why the martial artist merit would prove a mild balancing feature, but honestly, brawl doesn't provide charms, but martial arts do.<br /> <br /> The worst case scenario I can see is that DBT weakens your mastery level and certain combat charms have upgrades when in DBT. Of course I'd be pushing for being able to use martial arts in the iconic lunar combat mode but at the same time...<br /> <br /> Hm. I have no idea how to avoid martial arts being too good but also worthwhile to have. The combo capability is just really potent, like crazy potent. Add in that if Lunars have Lunar XP, then they can double dip into combat charms and martial arts charms...<br /> <br /> And since martial arts charms are balanced around other exalted, we're more likely to see Lunar charms have to be designed around martial arts, which might end up having martial arts being a missing piece to the lunar charmset.<br /> <br /> That said, I already mentioned a possible solution: Deadly Beastman Transformation might have Lunar practitioners use charms at Terrestrial level instead but many charms have bonuses when in DBT. Now this doesn't remove the option of karate bug monsterman, but it does discourage it enough to give clear intended combat styles and modes.<br /> <br /> I don't know. I'm rambling. I will say I am mildly concerned that Lunar charmsets might feel incomplete because they have to be designed around working with martial arts. My issue isn't that martial arts is good, its that I don't want the only way to make a combat lunar end up being &quot;take martial arts&quot;.<br /> <br /> So outside of the merit cost, why should a lunar use brawl?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, none of the styles in the core book, and likely none in the upcoming Dragon-Blooded book, are likely to be available to Lunars outside of human forms. Conversely, we might see some styles that work for specific beast forms and not for human form, and in the middle, some that have a mixed array of availability based on shape. Brawl, though... Brawl never changes, even if you do. Wailing on someone with reckless abandon is likely always appropriate to a Lunar's shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:41:23-08:00","id":1173307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173303#post1173303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, none of the styles in the core book, and likely none in the upcoming Dragon-Blooded book, are likely to be available to Lunars outside of human forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither is the Lunar's Brawl rating, since the Lunar uses the animal's Quick Character dice pools.<br /> <br /> The Lunar would have to buy a Charm that would substitute her human form's Dexterity + Brawl pool for those of her animal form's, when hers is better. A new incarnation of Internal Form Mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:55:03-08:00","id":1173315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173307#post1173307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither is the Lunar's Brawl rating, since the Lunar uses the animal's Quick Character dice pools.<br /> <br /> The Lunar would have to buy a Charm that would substitute her human form's Dexterity + Brawl pool for those of her animal form's, when hers is better. A new incarnation of Internal Form Mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not too sure that's something that you should be buying, since it kind of feels like an air-breathing mermaid function..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T13:59:52-08:00","id":1173319,"title":"","content":"If there isn't a Martial Art that grabs a player or is appropriate to the character, you'll probably be saving yourself a decent amount of XP by not buying extra Ability dots and Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T14:07:45-08:00","id":1173321,"title":"","content":"Well, presumably it'd be &quot;you can use your own pools instead of the animals if they are bigger&quot; (because &quot;you can attack with your own Dex+Brawl instead of the animals is probably too small a benefit; although admittedly Internal Form Mastery was only Dex before), and turning into a spider which is as strong as a human is definitely something that should need a charm purchase.<br /> <br /> Or, indeed, just turning into a fly that is as good on decisive attacks as a human (if it was only attack rolls), which is what Sunder's suggested charm does. That's pretty brutal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T14:21:13-08:00","id":1173325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173321#post1173321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, presumably it'd be &quot;you can use your own pools instead of the animals if they are bigger&quot; (because &quot;you can attack with your own Dex+Brawl instead of the animals is probably too small a benefit; although admittedly Internal Form Mastery was only Dex before), and turning into a spider which is as strong as a human is definitely something that should need a charm purchase.<br /> <br /> Or, indeed, just turning into a fly that is as good on decisive attacks as a human (if it was only attack rolls), which is what Sunder's suggested charm does. That's pretty brutal.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the stats for small animals are any indication, the main control on that is withering damage less than a typical light weapon. If the cat's bite is 4 and claw is 2 on withering damage, one would expect smaller animals to have 1 or 0 for withering damage, and require them to roll spectacularly just to match the cat's damage. Decisive attacks against larger beings might even simply be disallowed without setup gambits or Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T15:07:26-08:00","id":1173337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173286#post1173286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bAre you proposing that if the Styles had been put in a different book, they would have actually been written as something that the majority of players would be unable to use?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am proposing that the books Styles are included in correspond to design intent and likelihood in what characters are most likely to use them.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind those of us who collect all the books and keep track of where all given information can be found represent a tiny portion of players that are simply the most visible online because we talk about the game in our non-playing free time like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T15:36:32-08:00","id":1173348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173337#post1173337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am proposing that the books Styles are included in correspond to design intent and likelihood in what characters are most likely to use them.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind those of us who collect all the books and keep track of where all given information can be found represent a tiny portion of players that are simply the most visible online because we talk about the game in our non-playing free time like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOkaaaaayyy...<br /> <br /> \u200bglamourweaver, are you suggesting that there should be Martial Art Styles that are functionally exclusive to the Lunar Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T16:03:08-08:00","id":1173356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173348#post1173348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bOkaaaaayyy...<br /> <br /> \u200bglamourweaver, are you suggesting that there should be Martial Art Styles that are functionally exclusive to the Lunar Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and I have no idea what a I said that would give you that impression. I\u2019m suggesting that Martial Arts Styles that involve the use of non-human animal physical traits are going to get their most use of they\u2019re in the Lunar book. Of course Dragon Kings and other-types-of-Exalted Beastmen may also use said Styles, but Lunar players are going to make up the largest portion of players said Styles will be useful for (especially assuming the ability to swap out animal features as needed via the appropriate shapeshifting Charm).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T16:17:56-08:00","id":1173359,"title":"","content":"To put it more simply: which of the following would be most common assuming all 3E viable play materials were available?<br /> <br /> A) Pterok PCs<br /> <br /> B) Solar PCs with the \u201cWings\u201d Merit.<br /> <br /> C) Lunar PCs with winged Warforms and/or the Charms necessary to grow wings whenever they want.<br /> <br /> <br /> If the answer is \u201cC\u201d, and I think it is, then the Martial Arts Style built around winged aerial combat is going to get it\u2019s most use of it\u2019s in the Lunar book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T16:25:34-08:00","id":1173363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173356#post1173356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, and I have no idea what a I said that would give you that impression.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I knew you would say this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m suggesting that Martial Arts Styles that involve the use of non-human animal physical traits are going to get their most use of they\u2019re in the Lunar book. Of course Dragon Kings and other-types-of-Exalted Beastmen may also use said Styles, but Lunar players are going to make up the largest portion of players said Styles will be useful for (especially assuming the ability to swap out animal features as needed via the appropriate shapeshifting Charm).</div> </div> </div> </div>But the internal contradiction has admittedly thrown me for a bit of a loop.<br /> <br /> \u200bI find the idea of Martial Arts that are functionally exclusive to the Lunar Exalted on the basis of them being able to assume animal features to be contrary to the basic idea of Martial Arts, and imagine that few if any such traits would actually lend itself to very much of an actual Style.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T16:36:14-08:00","id":1173366,"title":"","content":"When I suggested the idea to Robert Vance, he didn't seem to like the idea of putting Dagger Wing Style or Black Depths Style in the Lunar manual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T16:45:18-08:00","id":1173369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173363#post1173363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I knew you would say this...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But the internal contradiction has admittedly thrown me for a bit of a loop.<br /> <br /> \u200bI find the idea of Martial Arts that are functionally exclusive to the Lunar Exalted on the basis of them being able to assume animal features to be contrary to the basic idea of Martial Arts, and imagine that few if any such traits would actually lend itself to very much of an actual Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>My basis for that notion is the very Martial Arts I first brought up. The Pterok style in 2E was usable by anyone who HAD WINGS. But since it was a Terrestrial Style, it got little use from people playing Celestial Exalted, so it was pretty much only used in the rare case of Pterok PCs. A Winged Martial Arts Style, USABLE BY ANY WINGED EXALTED, is inherently a cool concept if well executed, and I think the place it would get the most use would be if it was in the book with the Exalted who could most easily (BUT NOT EXCLUSIVELY) have wings.<br /> <br /> All the splat books are going to have Martial Arts Styles that for setting and/or mechanics-synchronicity reasons are going to be most used by the given splat, but it doesn\u2019t make them any less Martial Arts Styles potentialsely wieldable by any Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 01-05-2018, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T16:57:00-08:00","id":1173373,"title":"","content":"Since Martial Arts Styles are, as a general rule, developed by humanoids, and since we're highly unlikely to see a Martial Art Style developed for birds...<br /> <br /> I'd like to see a Martial Arts Style that tries to semi-realistically address what sorts of weapons would actually be used by winged humanoids.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eX02-O2dB9Q\" data-code=\"eX02-O2dB9Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/eX02-O2dB9Q/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T01:22:37-08:00","id":1173436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173369#post1173369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My basis for that notion is the very Martial Arts I first brought up. The Pterok style in 2E was usable by anyone who HAD WINGS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh I wish that so many of my books were not in storage.<br /> <br /> All right, my prior question was probably not clear enough. That's on me.<br /> <br /> \u200bWas Dagger Wing Style something that humans needed actual, functional wings for, or could they use it with the assistance of props that approximated wings?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Winged Martial Arts Style, USABLE BY ANY WINGED EXALTED, is inherently a cool concept if well executed</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the well executed part is the problem, as I think most concepts that could realise it as a Martial Art would be very thin, and that it's primarily being advocated for from the position of wanting something almost exclusive to Lunars (as other Exalted who are beastfolk are a bit of a marginal concept).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the splat books are going to have Martial Arts Styles that for setting and/or mechanics-synchronicity reasons are going to be most used by the given splat, but it doesn\u2019t make them any less Martial Arts Styles potentialsely wieldable by any Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bUnless the Immaculate Dragon Styles require dramatic transformations of characters in order to learn and use, that's not in the same boat as a Style that requires you to grow actual wings.<br /> <br /> \u200bGoing by the example of Silver-Voiced Nightingale, a transformation of that degree seems like it should be something inherent to the Martial Art, rather than functioning as a gateway to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T01:32:13-08:00","id":1173440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173302#post1173302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, this also touches on another possible mild issue. Why use brawl? I imagine that this is yet another reason why the martial artist merit would prove a mild balancing feature, but honestly, brawl doesn't provide charms, but martial arts do.<br /> <br /> The worst case scenario I can see is that DBT weakens your mastery level and certain combat charms have upgrades when in DBT. Of course I'd be pushing for being able to use martial arts in the iconic lunar combat mode but at the same time...<br /> <br /> Hm. I have no idea how to avoid martial arts being too good but also worthwhile to have. The combo capability is just really potent, like crazy potent. Add in that if Lunars have Lunar XP, then they can double dip into combat charms and martial arts charms...<br /> <br /> And since martial arts charms are balanced around other exalted, we're more likely to see Lunar charms have to be designed around martial arts, which might end up having martial arts being a missing piece to the lunar charmset.<br /> <br /> That said, I already mentioned a possible solution: Deadly Beastman Transformation might have Lunar practitioners use charms at Terrestrial level instead but many charms have bonuses when in DBT. Now this doesn't remove the option of karate bug monsterman, but it does discourage it enough to give clear intended combat styles and modes.<br /> <br /> I don't know. I'm rambling. I will say I am mildly concerned that Lunar charmsets might feel incomplete because they have to be designed around working with martial arts. My issue isn't that martial arts is good, its that I don't want the only way to make a combat lunar end up being &amp;quot;take martial arts&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> So outside of the merit cost, why should a lunar use brawl?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, maybe some Brawl charms get an upgrade when DBT is active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T01:40:57-08:00","id":1173443,"title":"","content":"Also, concerning Martial Arts Mastery effects, Lunars don\u2019t get the easy mastery effects of the Solars or the difficult mastery of the Sidereals. Why would you want to penalise them even further in DBT?<br /> <br /> Though I would get such a kick out of it if they did have some way to get Mastery in Animal specific Martial Arts like Monkey or Tiger. That would make my day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T06:01:36-08:00","id":1173471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173440#post1173440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, maybe some Brawl charms get an upgrade when DBT is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBut Lunars don't have Brawl Charms, and going by the premise of this thread, it doesn't even seem as though they would have combat Attribute Charms tied exclusively to Brawl either.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean sure, that's the other possibility for how to limit them if found to be broken in playtesting, to make some Charms that specify Brawl as the Ability they go with, although that would be one I would be more dubious on given the concept of Attribute Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you want to penalise them even further in DBT?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bDeadly Beastman Transformation has historically had an issue in which the benefits it provides and the minor investment it is to take it makes it kind of mandatory as a thing for Lunars to have and for them to conduct combat in. Both prior and current development teams have expressed views to the effect of this being undesirable.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt also has the advantage in which its concept of transforming into a synthesis of beast and human can naturally convey a basis for its own limitations, such as the idea that the shift in mindset is incompatible with things such as refined fighting styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T06:34:06-08:00","id":1173481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173440#post1173440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, maybe some Brawl charms get an upgrade when DBT is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator is right, they don't have Brawl charms. I replied to ScarecrowJ on the assumption he was referring to &quot;why use the Brawl ability when you could use the Martial Arts ability&quot;, since Martial Arts has charms, and Brawl does not.<br /> <br /> Hence the discussion about whether Lunars could use their own dice pools instead of their form's, since then Brawl would be better than Martial Arts (as using your Dex+Brawl with bear claws works, but Dex+Martial Arts does not, as bear claws are not valid weapons for any MA).<br /> <br /> As to the Winged MA, I think it's just too niche. Maybe if they were doing an entire book of MA, but I'd prefer to see some animal styles.<br /> (Lunar charms for flying combat though, absolutely.)<br /> <br /> On that subject:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I would get such a kick out of it if they did have some way to get Mastery in Animal specific Martial Arts like Monkey or Tiger. That would make my day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really want them to have some kind of natural benefit with Animal styles over other styles, but I can't really see a way to balance it well. <br /> <br /> My ideal would be to say they Favour animal styles but not other styles. But I'm not sure people would like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bDeadly Beastman Transformation has historically had an issue in which the benefits it provides and the minor investment it is to take it makes it kind of mandatory as a thing for Lunars to have and for them to conduct combat in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much so. I'm not sure I've seen a Lunar that doesn't use DBT in combat. I much prefer fighting as a bear (it's more stylish) but in 2e, DBT was the better choice mechanically.<br /> Admittedly, I think there's other ways to incentivise non-DBT; first off, the way animals are just better this edition. On the other hand, their attack pools are lower than DBT generally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T06:44:02-08:00","id":1173483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173436#post1173436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was Dagger Wing Style something that humans needed actual, functional wings for, or could they use it with the assistance of props that approximated wings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dagger Win<b>d</b> Style prequired <i>flight capable wings </i>and two dots in Athletics. (Debris of Fallen Races page 9)<br /> <br /> It does not explicitly mention whether or not \u200bArtefact wings would suffice, though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 01-05-2018, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T07:06:20-08:00","id":1173484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173471#post1173471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bDeadly Beastman Transformation has historically had an issue in which the benefits it provides and the minor investment it is to take it makes it kind of mandatory as a thing for Lunars to have and for them to conduct combat in. Both prior and current development teams have expressed views to the effect of this being undesirable.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt also has the advantage in which its concept of transforming into a synthesis of beast and human can naturally convey a basis for its own limitations, such as the idea that the shift in mindset is incompatible with things such as refined fighting styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I counter that if, for example, a Lunar Moonsilver swordsman wants to be a master of his weapon-craft and it's myriad Evocations, then he'd possibly think twice about DBT.<br /> <br /> For the Lunar Martial Artist, the lack of all Mastery effects, as things currently stand, kind of make them not quite as good at it as the Solars or Sidereals (though the free-form native charm combining might prove me a liar there). DBT does give them a brawny edge, but is it better than Mastery effects? I can't say.<br /> <br /> But I do see your point/worry. I for one would also like for there to be options, but, as I'm sure you wish as well, I also want DBT to be awesome.<br /> <br /> Maybe it'll be like so:<br /> <br /> Human - Best at evocations (possibly sorcery?)<br /> Animal - Easiest access to Legendary size, tiny merits. Versatility through shifting into different shapes.<br /> DBT- The form you take when you want to rip something apart with your bare hands (whether via native dex/str charms or Martial arts).<br /> <br /> Naive perhaps, but you gotta start somewhere.<br /> <br /> prototype00<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T07:21:33-08:00","id":1173485,"title":"","content":"So one thing we know is that there is no more wyld taint. However, I believe we still have Ma-Ha-Suchi in his full wolf-goat-human glory. This will be achieved via lunar charms by choice this time around.<br /> <br /> What if this gives some kind of material benefit when combined with appropriate styles? Perhaps Ma-Ha-Suchi chooses to be a goat-wolf-man because he's a master of Goat-style and wolf-style(note: afaik these styles do not currently exist) and really likes the combination of those styles with each other and his lunar charms?<br /> <br /> Perhaps not up to the level of unlocking mastery effects for a limited number of styles but there could be potential there as well. This is all pure speculation on my part of course other than the first paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T07:54:08-08:00","id":1173488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173481#post1173481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I really want them to have some kind of natural benefit with Animal styles over other styles, but I can't really see a way to balance it well.<br /> <br /> My ideal would be to say they Favour animal styles but not other styles. But I'm not sure people would like that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel as though this touches on a similar issue to the idea of a Martial Art that requires you to have some exclusive anatomical features, in that it grates a bit against the variety in Styles that is part of their appeal.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs a basic example, White Reaper Style has always had an association with Lunars, initially by it being the signature of Lilith, and then by Second Edition actually giving it a write-up in Glories: Luna with a backstory of being invented by a Lunar. Even in an Edition where such a backstory no longer strictly applies, in its imagery and its concept, there is a fairly strong resonance with Lunars there, and I think that to come out with an idea that the association is strictly inferior to an animal Style would hurt that.<br /> <br /> \u200bIndeed, while I advocate for the significance of animals to Lunars, I think there are problems with leaning too heavily on that, and I think that making them strictly superior at those Martial Arts would be a good example of that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it would be a better idea for their association with Martial Arts to be consistent across the board, and that it's enough of a contrast to Solar and Sidereal Mastery for them to be able to combine the Styles with their own powers.<br /> <br /> \u200bAfter all, I presume that's not just things like Strength and Dexterity; it might be that you get some potent effects from adding Lunar Manipulation and Appearance to Black Claw Style (another one that I think has some stylistic resonance with Lunars in its own right).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">want DBT to be awesome</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCertainly I'm not saying that it should be bad, just that it would need something to prevent it from being uniform for Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bHonesty, even the idea of it lowering their affinity for Magical Materials... that's not nothing, but I don't think it's huge either. Resonance and Dissonance are a nice way of ultimately representing different affinities for the Magical Materials, but per existing examples the differences are not very major, at least to my eyes. There are still plenty of Artifacts where even being Dissonant with it will allow you to wield some fairly potent effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Ma-Ha-Suchi chooses to be a goat-wolf-man because he's a master of Goat-style and wolf-style(note: afaik these styles do not currently exist) and really likes the combination of those styles with each other and his lunar charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think there was some talk a while back of there being some particular powers or benefits distinct to chimeras? I definitely don't think that the process or decision should hinge on a desire for certain Martial Arts mastery.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T08:13:10-08:00","id":1173490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173488#post1173488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI think there was some talk a while back of there being some particular powers or benefits distinct to chimeras? I definitely don't think that the process or decision should hinge on a desire for certain Martial Arts mastery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not married to the idea either, but figured it would be a way to explain why some choose the chimera route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T08:46:06-08:00","id":1173496,"title":"","content":"We know chimerism is a charm. They have distinct powers called &quot;Charms with that charm as a prerequisite&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T08:52:57-08:00","id":1173498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173471#post1173471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bBut Lunars don't have Brawl Charms, and going by the premise of this thread, it doesn't even seem as though they would have combat Attribute Charms tied exclusively to Brawl either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doi. Had a brain fart and temporarily forgot that for a second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T12:52:28-08:00","id":1173551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173496#post1173496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know chimerism is a charm. They have distinct powers called &amp;quot;Charms with that charm as a prerequisite&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another thing I think people are forgetting. Lunars have charms. In fact that's the entire point of this thread is Lunars can combo native charms with martial arts. Which is huge.<br /> <br /> If done poorly, every lunar is better if they grab the martial artist merit. I don't want that. I don't want to make a lunar character and feel like I MUST take martial arts to be awesome. I want to be able to take martial arts because I think that's cool.<br /> <br /> I have the same stance with DBT. I don't want DBT to be the absolute Lunar combat strategy like it was in 2e.<br /> <br /> I want is Lunars to have multiple flashy awesome ways to get into a fight. Whether that's with awesome artifacts, awesome martial arts, awesome unions of beast and man or my biggest concern: awesome native charms.<br /> <br /> My whole &quot;weaker martial arts in DBT&quot; idea had a second half to it: stronger native charms in DBT. The basis I had was simple: how do you encourage Lunars to not 100% without fail jump on martial arts as hard as a Siderial with a closed charmset?<br /> <br /> I don't want Lunars to suck at martial arts. I don't want martial arts to be a 100% straight upgrade on being lunar. I want there to be at least a choice in the manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T13:04:38-08:00","id":1173555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ScarecrowJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173551#post1173551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If done poorly, every lunar is better if they grab the martial artist merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>By the same logic, every Lunar is better if they have an artifact and invest in Evocations, and every Lunar is better if they become a sorceror and invest in spells and workings.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts, Evocations, and Sorcery compete for Lunar XP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have the same stance with DBT. I don't want DBT to be the absolute Lunar combat strategy like it was in 2e. </div> </div> </div>This, I agree with.<br /> <br /> DBT is cool, and I want to play a character that uses it.<br /> <br /> But I also want to play a character that fights with dozens of animal forms in a single battle, like Beastboy.<br /> <br /> Or I want to have a dragon for a spirit shape and burninate the countryside and peasants without bothering with DBT (except when I'm trapped in close quarters).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T14:15:20-08:00","id":1173580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1173555#post1173555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the same logic, every Lunar is better if they have an artifact and invest in Evocations, and every Lunar is better if they become a sorceror and invest in spells and workings.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts, Evocations, and Sorcery compete for Lunar XP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This, I agree with.<br /> <br /> DBT is cool, and I want to play a character that uses it.<br /> <br /> But I also want to play a character that fights with dozens of animal forms in a single battle, like Beastboy.<br /> <br /> Or I want to have a dragon for a spirit shape and burninate the countryside and peasants without bothering with DBT (except when I'm trapped in close quarters).</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference between Evocations, martial arts and sorcery for most exalted is that Evocations are mostly designed to supplement the native capabilities of the exalt in question. Sorcery is usually its own thing with (apparently) native charms supplementing the methods of using sorcery.<br /> <br /> Martial arts for most Exalts is designed to be its own ability and to not have to combo with native exalt powers (Excellencies excluded). They tend to have a strong central mechanical and stylistic thesis that informs how they work. They tend to be their own workhorses that have a bit more kick to them.<br /> <br /> The main point is that they mostly are designed in mind that they won't be combining with native charms.... Okay... That's presumptuous of me to say I can speak on design intent with authority. They SEEM to be designed with the idea that they don't get to work with melee, brawl, archery or thrown charms.<br /> <br /> I am worried that because Attribute charms can supplement Martial Arts charms that problems arise. My biggest worry is that attribute charmsets end up with holes in them because they have to be designed to work with martial arts.<br /> <br /> Iunno, I'm mostly spitballing concerns and possible solutions because I over think everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8907-scarecrowj","name":"ScarecrowJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:19:18-08:00","id":1174332,"title":"","content":"I, for one, want DBT to be an absolute or near-absolute combat strategy for Lunars. <br /> <br /> But I want that absolute to be a build-a-beast of customizable options and paths up a tree of additional options. Perhaps even a significant chunk of character-creation resting in the definition of spirit beast and DBT. <br /> <br /> I think I'd be enthused if the old RLF was subsumed into this part as well - maybe your transformation was more mental or spiritual than physical; more attitude than muscle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Unrelated to DBT but related to Lunars and Martial Arts - would a MArt be useless if you turn into the creature that inspired the art, or one like it?<br /> <br /> Can I fight in Crane Style if I'm a Crane? Can I fight in Snake Style if I'm a Snake? Can I fight in Single Point style if I'm a Swordfish?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T12:28:12-08:00","id":1174336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1174332#post1174332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated to DBT but related to Lunars and Martial Arts - would a MArt be useless if you turn into the creature that inspired the art, or one like it?<br /> <br /> Can I fight in Crane Style if I'm a Crane? Can I fight in Snake Style if I'm a Snake? Can I fight in Single Point style if I'm a Swordfish?</div> </div> </div> </div>The old dev team, at least, reacted negatively to this idea when it was raised. Lunars emulate the fundamental essence of snakes by <i>turning into snakes; </i>Snake Style is &quot;what if we had a fighting style inspired by the movements of snakes,&quot; but is designed for humans to use (and it isn't exactly an omni-serpentine style; an anaconda's combat strategy is utterly foreign to Snake Style). For other animals it gets substantially goofier; what exactly does an actual crane have to do with Crane Style? Cranes hunt by spearing frogs with their beaks, not by hitting them so hard that they go home and rethink their lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T13:38:58-08:00","id":1174353,"title":"","content":"You might get away with tiger style as a tiger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T04:08:43-08:00","id":1174516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aretii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1174336#post1174336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The old dev team, at least, reacted negatively to this idea when it was raised. Lunars emulate the fundamental essence of snakes by <i>turning into snakes; </i>Snake Style is &quot;what if we had a fighting style inspired by the movements of snakes,&quot; but is designed for humans to use (and it isn't exactly an omni-serpentine style; an anaconda's combat strategy is utterly foreign to Snake Style). For other animals it gets substantially goofier; what exactly does an actual crane have to do with Crane Style? Cranes hunt by spearing frogs with their beaks, not by hitting them so hard that they go home and rethink their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be interesting to find out how different storytellers and gaming groups would interpret the idea.<br /> <br /> If it got a laugh and played up the drama, heck, I'd run with it. Single Point Swordfish is exactly the kind of stunt I'd concoct, just because the villains wouldn't see it coming or know how to react to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T05:42:50-08:00","id":1174527,"title":"","content":"Overall I'm against such shenanigans. Martial Arts are very clearly designed as systems of battle for a type of being, that emulate traits from a theme.<br /> A tiger stylist fighting a tiger is not a symmetrical fight in that sense, for example. So whoever is using a martial art kinda has to be of the proper shape to use it. A DBT lunar is fine if it remains largely humanoid.<br /> <br /> Now you want to develop a martial art for an animal? We can have that. Imagine adapting White Reaper to a mantis' body. And teaching it to a godblooded praying mantis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 01-09-2018, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T06:07:44-08:00","id":1174531,"title":"","content":"I think Martial Arts for animals are the innate and latent abilities you teach them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T06:25:41-08:00","id":1174537,"title":"","content":"Yeah that's the clear analog. It's their actual capacities and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T06:38:32-07:00","id":1196461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1174531#post1174531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Martial Arts for animals are the innate and latent abilities you teach them.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is likely the best approximation for actual animals, I think it would be feasible for a being with a human-like mind and intellect and access to an animal's shape to develop a martial art for that body instead of their human-like one. It would likely take quite some effort, as the Lunar had all their life prior to Exaltation to know and adapt to their human body, as well as being able to rely on ages of study and experimentation of what said body can do that resulted in all those martial arts. Still, doesn't seem to me as thing beyond a human-with-an-animal-body, let alone a superhuman-with-an-animal-body such as Lunar.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it would take a pretty eccentric Lunar to go for that. Still, if you <b>do</b> have a Martial Arts master that spend the last two centuries living as a ram, they just might have developed Swift-Hoof Style and Horned-Thunder Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T10:25:25-07:00","id":1196525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1172699-lunar-martial-artists-just-got-a-lot-more-interesting-to-me?p=1196461#post1196461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that is likely the best approximation for actual animals, I think it would be feasible for a being with a human-like mind and intellect and access to an animal's shape to develop a martial art for that body instead of their human-like one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. They would develop new Merits, Abilities, and special attacks. That's enough like a Martial Arts Style.<br /> <br /> If they're actually a Lunar, they learn Lunar Charms. If they're actually a non-god spirit, they learn spirit Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}